# Directory Organization Limits — `actions`

Apply this rule for all code-change tasks.

## Structure principles

- Avoid large flat folders with many mixed files.
- Group files by domain/responsibility and keep related code together.
- Do not use a single catch-all `utils` directory for unrelated helpers.
- Prefer categorized utility folders (for example `utils/date`, `utils/format`, `utils/web3`) or domain-local helpers.

## Reorganization threshold

- When a directory reaches around 15-20 files, evaluate whether it should be split into focused subdirectories.
- If growth trend indicates fast expansion, proactively create categories earlier.

## Refactor safety

- Any folder reorganization must include all required path/import updates in the same change.
- Do not leave broken references, stale aliases, or partial moves.
